WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:04.768
Next Word. How a ChatGPT writes, one word at a
time.

00:06.968 --> 00:15.578
This machine read three short texts, about school and about science,
and counted which word usually comes after each word.

00:15.628 --> 00:21.257
That is all. It does not know grammar, and it
does not know what the words mean.

00:22.107 --> 00:24.135
I write a beginning: the teacher.

00:24.185 --> 00:29.299
On the right are the words it has seen after
teacher, with the chance of each one.

00:29.349 --> 00:32.763
The word says comes up more than a quarter of
the time.

00:33.613 --> 00:38.025
I can choose the next word myself, or let the
machine draw one.

00:38.075 --> 00:44.116
With each click, it looks at the last word,
checks its counts, and draws the next one.

00:44.966 --> 00:48.855
Now the creativity, which the experts call
temperature.

00:48.905 --> 00:52.293
At zero, it always picks the most probable
word.

00:52.343 --> 00:57.880
And then the text goes around in circles: the
class to the class to the class.

00:58.730 --> 01:02.564
With a high temperature, it takes risks on
rare words.

01:02.614 --> 01:08.246
The words still come from the text it read,
but the sentence loses its meaning.

01:09.096 --> 01:11.732
And how many words does it look back?

01:11.782 --> 01:17.903
Looking at only one, it has several options
and is drawing, as the green label shows.

01:17.953 --> 01:21.242
Looking at three, the sentences come out neat.

01:21.292 --> 01:25.235
But look at the label: one option, almost all
the time.

01:25.285 --> 01:27.486
It is copying the text it read.

01:28.336 --> 01:32.718
Any text works: a poem, a textbook chapter, a
course syllabus.

01:32.768 --> 01:37.579
I clear the text box, paste a new text, and
train the machine again.

01:37.629 --> 01:40.438
Now it writes in the style of that text.

01:41.288 --> 01:44.706
A ChatGPT does the same thing, at another
scale.

01:44.756 --> 01:50.270
It has read trillions of words and looks
hundreds of thousands of words back.

01:50.320 --> 01:52.438
That is why it writes so well.

01:52.488 --> 02:00.603
And that is also why it makes things up with the same confidence:
it chooses the probable word, not the true one.
